<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine firms buys 35,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Philippine firms buys 35,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Philippine flour mills bought a total of 35,000 tonnes U.S. wheat, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The firms bought 28,750 tonnes of dark northern spring wheat and 6,250 tonnes of western white wheat for January 1997 delivery on Wednesday night, they said.</p>
<p>The price at which the firms bought the wheat was not immediately available.</p>
<p>One trader involved in the deal however said the wheat was bought at &quot;very high levels.&quot;</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
